  "id": "COMPOUND:30135 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Tenacissoside B is implicated in the pathogenesis of VMRC-MELG through a multi-tiered mechanism involving the target proteins Prelamin-A/C, Oleamide, and Diplotrin A. The evidence suggests that Tenacissoside B acts as a modulator of these proteins, which in turn interact with VMRC-MELG. This pathway is supported by a consistent score of 0.5127 across three distinct paths, indicating a plausible and robust relationship. The shared target of Prelamin-A/C across all three paths suggests a common biological role, potentially in cellular structure or function. The involvement of different downstream targets (Oleamide and Diplotrin A) adds complexity, possibly reflecting diverse mechanisms of action or varying degrees of interaction with VMRC-MELG. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Tenacissoside B to influence VMRC-MELG through multiple, interconnected molecular mechanisms, which could be relevant in understanding its therapeutic effects or pathophysiological role.",
